    {
      "type": "examAlert",
      "items": [
        "Residuary powers of legislation lie strictly with Parliament, unlike in the United States where they belong to the states.",
        "Distinguish carefully between Federal Features (Dual Polity, Written Constitution, Independent Judiciary) and Unitary Features (Single Citizenship, Integrated Judiciary, Emergency Provisions).",
        "Article 249 empowers Parliament to legislate on a State List subject in the national interest upon a Rajya Sabha resolution.",
        "Inter-state water disputes under Article 262 are outside the jurisdiction of the Supreme Court."
      ],
      "id": "ne137r8"
